      "confidence": 0.9,
      "curator_note": "Concrete: fluoroethane molecular ion CH3-CH2-F(+.) loses H. to give the fluoronium ion CH3-CH=F(+); this is the dominant of the two competing channels (100%, dH = 0.2 eV) and the H. lost comes from the F-bearing carbon (C2), so a C2=F(+) pi bond forms. The book explicitly frames this R(+.)R'Y -> R. + R'Y(+) pathway as the ground state of the products correlating with an EXCITED state of M(+.), and distinguishes it from initial heteroatom (inductive) ionization; charge+radical are localized on F here only to give the alpha-cleavage arrows a real origin (encoding convention B). Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: equation 8.40 is printed as a plain net-reaction line 'H(+)CH(CH3)F -> H. + CH3CH=F(+) (100%)'. All three moves <1,2,3> are curator-supplied to balance the alpha C-H homolysis and are NOT drawn on the page: (1) the F(+.) odd electron into the forming C2=F pi bond, (2) one electron of the C2-H sigma bond into that same pi bond, (3) the second C2-H electron onto the departing H.."
    },
